": 4,\n        \"text\": \"Poor\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"variants\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"custom\",\n      \"name\": \"corridor_assessment\",\n      \"title\": \"Assess the brightness and uniformity of the corridor lighting\",\n      \"isRequired\": false,\n      \"description\": \"Ten computer visualisations (Autodesk 3ds Max, luminance checked against DIALux) of the same empty corridor lit by six luminaire types in ten layouts (direct downlights, continuous or broken light lines, direct-indirect and indirect luminaires), shown one after another in the paper's order (variant 1 to 10). For each variant: brightness and uniformity of the ceiling, walls, floor and the entire corridor on 7-point semantic differential scales (Extremely bright … Extremely dim; Extremely uniform … Extremely non-uniform). Value: {ceiling_brightness, ceiling_uniformity, walls_…, floor_…, corridor_…}, coded as in the paper: 7 = extremely bright / extremely uniform, 1 = extremely dim / extremely non-uniform. Analysis as in the paper: mean, median, min, max, SD per variant and plane; compare groups or viewing conditions with the Wald–Wolfowitz runs test.\",\n      \"items\": [\n       {\n        \"key\": \"ceiling_brightness\",\n        \"plane\": \"Assess ceiling brightness and uniformity in the corridor\",\n        \"feature\": \"brightness\",\n        \"levels\": [\n         \"Extremely bright\",\n         \"Very bright\",\n         \"Rather bright\",\n         \"Moderate\",\n         \"Rather dim\",\n         \"Very dim\",\n         \"Extremely dim\"\n        ]\n       },\n       {\n        \"key\": \"ceiling_uniformity\",\n        \"plane\": \"Assess ceiling brightness and uniformity in the corridor\",\n        \"feature\": \"uniformity\",\n        \"levels\": [\n         \"Extremely uniform\",\n         \"Very uniform\",\n         \"Rather uniform\",\n         \"Moderate\",\n         \"Rather non-uniform\",\n         \"Very non-uniform\",\n         \"Extremely non-uniform\"\n        ]\n       },\n       {\n        \"key\": \"walls_brightness\",\n        \"plane\": \"Assess wall brightness and uniformity in the corridor\",\n        \"feature\": \"brightness\",\n        \"levels\": [\n         \"Extremely bright\",\n         \"Very bright\",\n         \"Rather bright\",\n         \"Moderate\",\n         \"Rather dim\",\n         \"Very dim\",\n         \"Extremely dim\"\n        ]\n       },\n       {\n        \"key\": \"walls_uniformity\",\n        \"plane\": \"Assess wall brightness and uniformity in the corridor\",\n        \"feature\": \"uniformity\",\n        \"levels\": [\n         \"Extremely uniform\",\n         \"Very uniform\",\n         \"Rather uniform\",\n         \"Moderate\",\n         \"Rather non-uniform\",\n         \"Very non-uniform\",\n         \"Extremely non-uniform\"\n        ]\n       },\n       {\n        \"key\": \"floor_brightness\",\n        \"plane\": \"Assess floor brightness and uniformity in the corridor\",\n        \"feature\": \"brightness\",\n        \"levels\": [\n         \"Extremely bright\",\n         \"Very bright\",\n         \"Rather bright\",\n         \"Moderate\",\n         \"Rather dim\",\n         \"Very dim\",\n         \"Extremely dim\"\n        ]\n       },\n       {\n        \"key\": \"floor_uniformity\",\n        \"plane\": \"Assess floor brightness and uniformity in the corridor\",\n        \"feature\": \"uniformity\",\n        \"levels\": [\n         \"Extremely uniform\",\n         \"Very uniform\",\n         \"Rather uniform\",\n         \"Moderate\",\n         \"Rather non-uniform\",\n         \"Very non-uniform\",\n         \"Extremely non-uniform\"\n        ]\n       },\n       {\n        \"key\": \"corridor_brightness\",\n        \"plane\": \"Assess brightness and uniformity of the entire corridor\",\n        \"feature\": \"brightness\",\n        \"levels\": [\n         \"Extremely bright\",\n         \"Very bright\",\n     